{"wireMagic": "pb3", "events": [{"tStartMs": 0, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "[Music]"}]}, {"tStartMs": 5000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "Welcome to lecture three on graph algorithms."}]}, {"tStartMs": 60000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "Today we study breadth-first search and depth-first search."}]}, {"tStartMs": 100000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "A graph is a set of vertices connected by edges."}]}, {"tStartMs": 130000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "Breadth-first search explores the graph level by level using a queue."}]}, {"tStartMs": 200000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "It finds shortest paths in unweighted graphs."}]}, {"tStartMs": 310000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "Depth-first search goes deep first using a stack or recursion."}]}, {"tStartMs": 400000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "Depth-first search is useful for topological sorting and cycle detection."}]}, {"tStartMs": 590000, "dDurationMs": 4000, "segs": [{"utf8": "That is all for today, thanks for watching."}]}]}